 "notes": {
  "forAnalyst": "Request for quote: a buyer asks for a price, a sales person answers, and an agreed quote becomes an order. The B2B negotiation step that B2C does not have.",
  "forArchitect": "Thirteen required dependencies — the second most coupled module in the catalogue after Orders — because a quote spans catalog, pricing, cart, order, customer and notifications. Eight entities and 34 migrations of its own, plus three GraphQL builders, so it is a full capability rather than a hook.",
  "forDeveloper": "A quote is its own document with its own status flow; do not model it as a cart with a flag. Three schema builders mean the storefront path is GraphQL, and one declared event is what downstream automation should subscribe to.",
  "owns": [
   "QuoteRequestEntity"
  ],
  "reachForItWhen": [
   "Prices are negotiated rather than published",
   "A sales person must approve or adjust before an order exists",
   "B2B buyers expect a quote document they can circulate internally"
  ],
  "doNotReachForItWhen": [
   "Prices are fixed — a cart plus a promotion is simpler",
   "You need the sale itself: a quote converts into an order, and the order is authoritative",
   "The host must stay small: thirteen dependencies make this a full commerce install"
  ]
 },
